WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.710
Let's do a reasoning exercise before writing more
SQL We have two

00:00:05.736 --> 00:00:10.029
versions of a condition In Version A age greater
than or equal

00:00:10.055 --> 00:00:15.454
to sixty-five is connected by OR to a
diagnosis-and-consent condition In Version

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.106
B age or diagnosis is grouped inside parentheses and
consent is required

00:00:20.132 --> 00:00:25.093
afterward Try to identify the patient who appears
only when the parentheses

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:29.191
are omitted A useful strategy is to look for an
older patient

00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:34.114
whose consent is false Ask yourself in Version A
does the consent

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:39.164
condition apply to the age branch Then compare that
with Version B

00:00:40.068 --> 00:00:43.006
You can test the related query in the browser from
the earlier

00:00:43.032 --> 00:00:48.579
slide or copy it into pgAdmin and modify it yourself
The

00:00:48.605 --> 00:00:51.182
goal here is to explain why the results differ
